# p5 mcp: what the model is told when a server refuses a call with a JSON-RPC
# error that carries `data` -- compact, spaced and reordered, and with a NUL
# (p5-mcp-errdata.sh). fx v0.0.16 keeps only the error's code and message
# (`CallResult.failure`, src/core/mcp_host/runtime.zig:117 and :2371@481104fd;
# `render`, src/core/mcp_host/model.zig:841), so its diagnostic writer, which
# would append `; data=` (src/core/mcp/tool_result.zig:199-214), never sees any.
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-errdata-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-errdata-profile.json
gateway p5-mcp-errdata-turns.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=full-access
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=yolo
wait 6
type call the refusing tool three times
key Enter
wait 10
snap turn
gwlog
